cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Version 3.0.0, 12 September 2026. Identify the version and informal AI-review status when citing."
title: "Positivity and explicit SoS size for bamboo-tree weak rank"
authors:
  - name: "Quantyra Research"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "For even q>=1024, input width N=8q+4, m=q^2, and D=floor(q/(32 log_2 q)), the unaugmented simple bamboo encoding of I_m requires explicit real SoS certificate size at least (8/7)^((2D-1)/2), hence exp(Omega(N/log N)), under the source's axiom-multiplier and square-root monomial convention. The proof establishes bounded-row-space square positivity and applies a credited random restriction to residual width q. Earlier full-variable ordinary-degree positivity and its exact degree corollary are preserved. Informal mathematics with AI-agent review; novelty and priority are unknown."
keywords:
  - weak rank principle
  - local distributions
  - conditional correlation
  - positivity
  - Boolean polynomials
  - sum of squares
  - certificate degree
  - certificate size
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: 2026-09-12
url: "https://github.com/Quantyra/weak-rank-positivity-window"
